   },
   {
    "id": "blockquote_00002",
    "type": "blockquote",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     13
    ],
    "text": "strtok, strtok_r — split string into tokens",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00003",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     15
    ],
    "text": "[A2][/A2]SYNOPSIS",
    "placeholders": {
     "A2": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_592_02\" id=\"tag_17_592_02\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00004",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     17,
     1
    ],
    "text": "[CODE3]",
    "placeholders": {
     "CODE3": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<code><tt>#include &lt;<a href=\"../basedefs/string.h.html\">string.h</a>&gt;<br>\n<br>\nchar *strtok(char *restrict</tt> <i>s</i><tt>, const char *restrict</tt> <i>sep</i><tt>);<br></tt></code>"
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00005",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     19
    ],
    "text": "[A4][/A4]DESCRIPTION",
    "placeholders": {
     "A4": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_592_03\" id=\"tag_17_592_03\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00006",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     1
    ],
    "text": "For [I5]strtok[/I5](): [S6][[A7]CX[/A7]][/S6] [IMG8] &nbsp;The functionality described on this reference page is aligned with the ISO&nbsp;C standard. Any\nconflict between the requirements described here and the ISO&nbsp;C standard is unintentional. This volume of POSIX.1-2024 defers\nto the ISO&nbsp;C standard. [IMG9]",
    "placeholders": {
     "I5": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "S6": {
      "open": "<sup>",
      "close": "</sup>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A7": {
      "open": "<a href=\"javascript:open_code(&#x27;CX&#x27;)\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "IMG8": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<img src=\"../images/opt-start.gif\" alt=\"[Option Start]\" border=\"0\">"
     },
     "IMG9": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<img src=\"../images/opt-end.gif\" alt=\"[Option End]\" border=\"0\">"
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00007",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     3
    ],
    "text": "A sequence of calls to [I10]strtok[/I10]() breaks the string pointed to by [I11]s[/I11] into a sequence of tokens, each of which is\ndelimited by a byte from the string pointed to by [I12]sep[/I12]. The first call in the sequence has [I13]s[/I13] as its first argument,\nand is followed by calls with a null pointer as their first argument. The separator string pointed to by [I14]sep[/I14] may be\ndifferent from call to call.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I10": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I11": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I12": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I13": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I14": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00008",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     5
    ],
    "text": "The first call in the sequence searches the string pointed to by [I15]s[/I15] for the first byte that is [I16]not[/I16] contained in the\ncurrent separator string pointed to by [I17]sep[/I17]. If no such byte is found, then there are no tokens in the string pointed to by\n[I18]s[/I18] and [I19]strtok[/I19]() shall return a null pointer. If such a byte is found, it is the start of the first token.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I15": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I16": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I17": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I18": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I19": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00009",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     7
    ],
    "text": "The [I20]strtok[/I20]() function then searches from there for a byte that [I21]is[/I21] contained in the current separator string. If no\nsuch byte is found, the current token extends to the end of the string pointed to by [I22]s[/I22], and subsequent searches for a token\nshall return a null pointer. If such a byte is found, it is overwritten by a NUL character, which terminates the current token. The\n[I23]strtok[/I23]() function saves a pointer to the following byte, from which the next search for a token shall start.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I20": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I21": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I22": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I23": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00010",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     9
    ],
    "text": "Each subsequent call, with a null pointer as the value of the first argument, starts searching from the saved pointer and\nbehaves as described above.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00011",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     11
    ],
    "text": "The implementation shall behave as if no function defined in this volume of POSIX.1-2024 calls [I24]strtok[/I24]().",
    "placeholders": {
     "I24": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00012",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     13
    ],
    "text": "The [I25]strtok[/I25]() function need not be thread-safe; however, [I26]strtok[/I26]() shall avoid data races with all other\nfunctions.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I25": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I26": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00013",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     15
    ],
    "text": "[S27][[A28]CX[/A28]][/S27] [IMG29] The\n[I30]strtok_r[/I30]() function shall be equivalent to [I31]strtok[/I31](), except that [I32]strtok_r[/I32]() shall be thread-safe and the\nargument [I33]state[/I33] points to a user-provided pointer that allows [I34]strtok_r[/I34]() to maintain state between calls which scan\nthe same string. The application shall ensure that the pointer pointed to by [I35]state[/I35] is unique for each string ([I36]s[/I36])\nbeing processed concurrently by [I37]strtok_r[/I37]() calls. The application need not initialize the pointer pointed to by [I38]state[/I38]\nto any particular value. The implementation shall not update the pointer pointed to by [I39]state[/I39] to point (directly or\nindirectly) to resources, other than within the string [I40]s[/I40], that need to be freed or released by the caller. [IMG41]",
    "placeholders": {
     "S27": {
      "open": "<sup>",
      "close": "</sup>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A28": {
      "open": "<a href=\"javascript:open_code(&#x27;CX&#x27;)\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "IMG29": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<img src=\"../images/opt-start.gif\" alt=\"[Option Start]\" border=\"0\">"
     },
     "I30": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I31": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I32": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I33": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I34": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I35": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I36": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I37": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I38": {
      "open": "<i>",
