     2,
     29,
     1
    ],
    "text": "No errors are defined.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00020",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     35
    ],
    "text": "[A58][/A58]EXAMPLES",
    "placeholders": {
     "A58": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_592_06\" id=\"tag_17_592_06\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h5_00021",
    "type": "h5",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     37,
     1
    ],
    "text": "[A59][/A59]Searching for Word Separators",
    "placeholders": {
     "A59": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_592_06_01\" id=\"tag_17_592_06_01\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00022",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     37,
     3
    ],
    "text": "The following example searches for tokens separated by &lt;space&gt; characters.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h5_00023",
    "type": "h5",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     37,
     7
    ],
    "text": "[A60][/A60]Find First two Fields in a Buffer",
    "placeholders": {
     "A60": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_592_06_02\" id=\"tag_17_592_06_02\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00024",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     37,
     9
    ],
    "text": "The following example uses [I61]strtok[/I61]() to find two character strings (a key and data associated with that key) separated by\nany combination of &lt;space&gt;, &lt;tab&gt;, or &lt;newline&gt; characters at the start of the array of characters pointed to by\n[I62]buffer[/I62].",
    "placeholders": {
     "I61": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I62": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00025",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     39
    ],
    "text": "[A63][/A63]APPLICATION USAGE",
    "placeholders": {
     "A63": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_592_07\" id=\"tag_17_592_07\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00026",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     41,
     1
    ],
    "text": "Note that if [I64]sep[/I64] is the empty string, [I65]strtok[/I65]() and [I66]strtok_r[/I66]() return a pointer to the remainder of the\nstring being tokenized.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I64": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I65": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I66": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00027",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     41,
     3
    ],
    "text": "The [I67]strtok_r[/I67]() function is thread-safe and stores its state in a user-supplied buffer instead of possibly using a static\ndata area that may be overwritten by an unrelated call from another thread.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I67": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00028",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     43
    ],
    "text": "[A68][/A68]RATIONALE",
    "placeholders": {
     "A68": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_592_08\" id=\"tag_17_592_08\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00029",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     45,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The [I69]strtok[/I69]() function searches for a separator string within a larger string. It returns a pointer to the last substring\nbetween separator strings. This function uses static storage to keep track of the current string position between calls. The new\nfunction, [I70]strtok_r[/I70](), takes an additional argument, [I71]state[/I71], to keep track of the current position in the string.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I69": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I70": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I71": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00030",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     47
    ],
